IN THE SUPREME COURT OF INDIA
CASE NO: Civil Appeal No. 5785 of 2019
CITATION: (2019) 19 SCC 161
YEAR: 2019

CORAM / BENCH:
Hon'ble Judges: Arun Mishra, U.U. Lalit

PARTIES:
Bikram Chatterjee vs Union of India

STATUTES & ACTS REFERRED:
Real Estate (Regulation and Development) Act, 2016, Insolvency and Bankruptcy Code, 2016

KEY PROVISIONS & SECTIONS:
Article 142, Section 8 RERA

LEGAL KEYWORDS & TOPICS:
diversion of homebuyer funds, nbcc completion, forensic audit, housing fraud

================================================================================
                    JUDGMENT SUMMARY & RATIO DECIDENDI
================================================================================

Exercised Article 142 powers to cancel RERA registration of Amrapali Group, ordering forensic audit and assigning stalled projects to NBCC to protect 42,000 homebuyers.

1. ISSUES CONSIDERED:
   The court addressed questions of legal interpretation under Article 142, Section 8 RERA.

2. ANALYSIS & PRECEDENT CONTEXT:
   Having examined the statutory scheme, fundamental principles of jurisprudence,
   and constitutional safeguards, the Court reiterated the necessity of strict
   compliance with statutory procedure and evidentiary standards.

3. HELD & BINDING RATIO:
   The principle formulated in this judgment constitutes binding judicial precedent
   within its territorial and appellate jurisdiction.

